  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Kartu Peserta Madrasah",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"Kartu Peserta Madrasah\"**\n\nEvery screen is a card the student holds: a white card stamped out of a deep madrasah-green band, with a printed header strip, small spaced capitals naming each field the way a student ID does (\"NO. URUT\", \"DIBUKA\", \"KODE BUKTI\"), a giant tabular number, a dashed tear line with half-moon notches, and a red round stamp once the vote is cast. The system answers to the madrasah's own logo: green shield, yellow wings, red-and-yellow frame, the *Iqra'* calligraphy.\n\nPages follow one structure. A full-width green ribbon (the header continues into a page band with a faint guilloche wave print) carries the page's display headline, and the first card pushes up into it from below with a negative overlap. Under it sits the \"mading\" (wall board): dense white modules hung from small coloured tabs. The layout stays light and phone-first: no photo banners, no hero imagery, no sidebars. Density comes from ruled lists with date blocks, not from cards nested in cards.\n\nThe build rejects the stock school portal (photo banner, grey-white cards, sidebar) and the stock SaaS look of the starter kit; neutral zinc/grey is not part of the student-facing world.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A green ribbon owns the head of every page, and a card overlaps it from below.",
      "White cards with a 14px radius, a 1px green-grey hairline, and a deep green-tinted drop.",
      "Field labels in narrow, spaced capitals; values set bold in ink green.",
      "Giant tabular numerals for ballot numbers, dates and percentages.",
      "Yellow is for the one primary action, the active nav state, and the main mading tab.",
      "Red appears only as the stamp and as error text."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Stamp Red Rule",
        "body": "Frame red is the stamp's ink. Outside the stamp it only marks an error or a destructive action. It never decorates, never fills a button, never appears on a chip.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Gold Action Rule",
        "body": "A view has at most one gold button. Other actions are green, white-with-hairline, or the dashed locked state.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Green-Tinted Neutral Rule",
        "body": "Text, lines and shadows use the green-tinted ink, hairline and rgb(4 41 26) shadow tint. Zinc, grey and black do not appear in student-facing screens.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Field Label Rule",
        "body": "Spaced narrow capitals name a field and sit directly above its value (a `dt`), or they name the card in its header strip. They never float above a section heading as an eyebrow.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Number Rule",
        "body": "Every number a student compares (ballot number, time, date, vote count, percentage) is tabular.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Over Green Rule",
